Subject: [PATCH 02242/11362] [outer-loop] clarify offline submission: weights
 bundled as Kaggle dataset, mounted at /kaggle/input

'No internet' blocks hosted-API calls, NOT local file reads. Trained weights (TRM ckpt /
GGUF) upload once as a Kaggle Dataset, mount read-only in the offline sandbox, load from
disk -> a LOCAL model is offline-legal precisely because it's a bundled FILE. Two findings:
(1) prize-eligible license is CC0/MIT-0 (stricter than Apache-2.0) -- action item;
(2) a possible third-party-compute call-out (~$10k cap) seen in ARC-AGI-2 is UNCONFIRMED
for ARC-AGI-3 -- verify before relying on it.

